        "Paul answers the rejection question negatively, identifies himself as Israelite, and cites Elijah's preserved remnant.",
        "Directly contradicts claims that God rejected Jews as a people or transferred their identity to gentile Christians without remainder.",
        "Romans rejects the proposition that Israel stumbled in order to fall and relates the present sequence to gentile inclusion and Israel's fullness.",
        "Prevents present disagreement from becoming a theology of permanent Jewish abandonment."
